 "notes": [
  "Tree crowns read from the 2026-05-26 aerial (Wayback release 2026-10-29, Vantor Vivid Advanced, May 2026 z19 tiles): [x, z, crown width in metres], world metres, +X east, +Z south. Production inference, not survey data: crowns of dark, textured canopy on the land, split at the peaks of a distance transform; positions are good to about 5 m (the imagery sits 3-6 m off OSM in places), and a clump may be several trees or one.",
  "Audited by eye against the same aerial: dark roofs, a tank, asphalt and bare ground the mask read as crowns are gone, and sparse and bright crowns it missed are added by hand (the mask finds dark canopy only), so a clump here is one or several trees as seen.",
  "Groups name the areas a street-detail canopy rule plants (tools/config/street-detail-zones.json); species are the rules' mixes, not read from the aerial. Round tanks, ponds and the zones planted by their own rules are left out. fourth_street_lot_palms is traced palm by palm.",
  "Hedges: lines 1.5 m out from the walls where dark foliage runs along them in the same aerial, 5 m or more long, about two runs in five kept (the rest of what the aerial shows there is yard shrubs) and opened every 7 m or so: the data does not place the unit entries, which a hedge must not cross."
 ],
